hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1243","Ali bin Hajar Al-Saadi told us once, Jarir told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “He would pray sitting, and when there were thirty or forty verses of the Surah remaining for him, he would stand up and recite them, then bow.”"
"1244","Yaqoub Al-Dawraqi, Ibn Ulayya, told us, Al-Walid Ibn Abi Hisham, H., Ma’mal Ibn Hisham, and Ziyad Ibn Ayyub told us, saying: Ismail told us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amra, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God was May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He recites while sitting, then when he wants to kneel, he stands as long as a person recites forty verses.”"
